                <pb facs="0264" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/267a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Yokohama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Scidmore</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-24T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1917, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For John F. Stevens from Daniel Willard: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Your cable 20th. Understand you are with Emerson and his force at Nagasaki. It is thought best
                            that you should all remain there for a while and await developments in
                            Russia. Probably inside thirty days definite decision can be reached
                            concerning future course. There is great opportunity for most valuable
                            work for you and Emerson in
                            Russia, providing stable government is established and think it would be
                            most unfortunate to abandon that plan as long as there is any hope. Have
                            had credit established for you as per your cable December 4 and $50,000
                            for Emerson. Assume this will
                            keep you both going until definite decision can be reached concerning
                            future. Keep me advised any new developments.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>If Stevens not at Yokohama forward the
                    above to Nagasaki.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
